Package: druidos-hive
Architecture: amd64
Depends: ${shlibs:Depends}, ${misc:Depends}
Recommends: zfsutils-linux
Suggests: druidos-hive-docs
Description: DruidOS Hive Stack - AI-assisted system monitoring
 DruidOS is a Linux distribution with an integrated Small Language Model
 that acts as a living consciousness observing the system in real-time.
 .
 This package contains the core Hive Stack components:
  - hive-cortex: Central orchestrator daemon
  - hive-synapse: SLM inference daemon
  - hive-actuator: Action executor
  - hive-nerve-*: System observers
  - hive-apt: Intelligent apt wrapper
  - hive-zfs: ZFS snapshot management
  - grove: Interactive shell (primary user interface)
  - hive-dashboard: Interactive TUI panel for notifications/suggestions

Package: druidos-hive-docs
Architecture: all
Description: DruidOS Hive Stack Documentation
 Documentation for the DruidOS Hive Stack including:
  - Architecture overview
  - Security model
  - User guide
  - API documentation

Package: druidos-config
Architecture: all
Depends: druidos-hive
Description: DruidOS Default Configuration
 Default configuration files for DruidOS including:
  - Hive Stack configuration
  - Systemd service files

Package: druidos-knowledge
Architecture: all
Depends: druidos-hive
Description: DruidOS Knowledge Base
 Knowledge base files for the Hive Stack including:
  - Package knowledge (installation notes, warnings)
  - Command patterns (dangerous command detection)
  - Error patterns (common issue recognition)
